  {
    "equipment_id": "5353",
    "equipment_eq_id": "EQ ID 5353",
    "equipment_name": "Tenoner",
    "department": "Toilet Partitions",
    "wo_id": "17515",
    "date_notified": "10/29/2025",
    "urgency": "1. Prod Stopped",
    "problem": "The tenoner was having issues pulling pieces, which we diagnosed as most likely being the hold down wheels being too low. After raising them from 0.625\" to 0.635\" it was running smoother. Afterward the buffer wheels were determined to need swapping. The swap was performed and the tenoner was dialed in after multiple trial and error attempts. The hold down issue returned and was probably due to material warping. Tool left in tech mode to adjust hold down as needed.",
    "status": "Closed and Completed",
    "material_cost": "0",
    "labor_time": "4.5",
    "work_performed_by": "Nicholas Angelo Jr. and Jordon Dunn",
    "assigned_to": "Maintenance",
    "downtime_hours": "4.5",
    "completed_datetime": "10/29/2025 09:00 PM",
    "comments": "Nicholas Angelo, Jr - 10/29/25  7:03:09 PM: Hold down issue most likely is due to the variability of the material and the effect the outdoors has on it when stored there. As for the dialing in of the buffer wheels, this took longer than expected to achieve acceptable finishes on the edges of test pieces. An email has been sent notifying all vested parties.",
    "attachments": []
  },
